            "review_title": "Review at 4Gs Texas",
            "review_text": "Shaun M\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam299 contributions\n0\nFails To Deliver On Its Promise\nOct 2016 • Friends\nWalking into this restaurant which is up to the 1st floor after navigating your way through the ground floor bakery and variety store, one gets the sense that possibly we could be in for a wonderful meal experience. The menu is of a higher price than normal in HCMC and you will find images of authentic looking pizzas, pasta and range of steaks and lamb cutlets. I opted for the USA fillet and expected this to be pretty good. The presentation looked like it had been inspired by an episode of Masterchef with the little dribbles of sauce scattered around the outside of the plate. I was ready for something marvelous, but alas, the steak was difficult to cut into even with the steak knife, and it was hard work to chew. The accompanying vegetables were under cooked, semi cooked whole onions, semi cooked garlic pieces and a watery mashed potato. It was truly disappointing. I thought I would try the desserts but was disappointed to find that only 3 of the 15 offerings were available tonight. Isn't this primarily a bakery????? The service was fine, a friendly man, who served everyone as the restaurant was busy, I wonder why? I think because they have not delivered on the promise of a fine Texan food experience. Oh well, another time!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 24, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
