            "review_text": "Tiim® Group\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam47 contributions\n0\nTerrible service and unacceptable charge\nJul 2015 • Couples\nI just had lunch here. No staff at entrance door. I entered and there were a couple of eyes looking at me from the inside hidden table, she just looked at me from away, no action. I stood there about 3 minutes without any coming staff. Then there was a staff stepped out and coming to me, but still no words. I asked her \"do you have set menu or a-la-carte?\" She asked back \"what kind of dish you want?\" I replied \"can you show me your menu?\" - \"yes\". Then I chose a table and sat down. She followed and asked me again \"what kind of dish you want?\". I again asked her \"please show me your menu\". She went away to take menu and shown me. I saw on the font door of the restaurant \"banh canh cua, special 65.000 vnd, normal 55.000 vnd, small 45.000 vnd\". I asked her \"do you have banh canh cua?\" she said \"yes\". Then I order \"1 normal please\". Then, when I settle the bill, I saw the bill charged me 65.000 vnd (price of special one). I asked her \"I just ordered the normal, not special\". She replied \"we only sell special\". I asked her \"why you did not tell me when I ordered?\". She kept silent. I paid 65.000 vnd. And I shall never come back.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 21, 2015",
